tbc (dx12-renderer): frame capture for offline replay, at the renderer's own interface, so it works in any game
(Skullburglar's capture.cpp hooks its game's D3D functions by address). Records, from one swap: the register file
and the non-zero pages of guest physical memory, then every draw (changed registers, shaders, draw), occlusion
query, end of frame and present, with the guest memory the renderer uploads at the moment it does and the ranges it
is told were written; and each frame's front buffer as the live renderer resolved it (ref_<n>.ppm).
BOTS_GFX_CAPTURE="<sec>[,<sec>...]" (from the first swap), BOTS_GFX_CAPTURE_FRAMES (default 3),
BOTS_GFX_CAPTURE_DIR (default gfxcap; <dir>/capture.now captures the next frame). Off unless one is set.
Needs native-plugin\CMakeLists.txt to list src/gfx/frame_capture.cpp. Format: src/gfx/frame_capture.h.

